  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\u03a0$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-1}{2}=\\frac{y+2}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{3},\\,\u03a0:r\\cdot \u27e81,6,2\u27e9=19.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(1,-2,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=\u27e82,1,3\u27e9.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\u27e81,-2,1\u27e9+t\u27e82,1,3\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81+2t,-2+t,1+3t\u27e9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=\u27e81+2t,-2+t,1+3t\u27e9$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot \u27e81,6,2\u27e9 & =19 \\\\ \u27e81+2t,-2+t,1+3t\u27e9\\cdot \u27e81,6,2\u27e9 & =19 \\\\ (1+2t)+6(-2+t)+2(1+3t) & =19 \\\\ 1+2t-12+6t+2+6t & =19 \\\\ 14t & =28 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\u27e81+2(2),-2+2,1+3(2)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e85,0,7\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(5,0,7).$",
